// ── v6.2: NUCLEAR SYNC ENGINE CONFIG (four-layer design) ──────────
//
//  v6.2 is a complete rewrite of the sync engine.  The v6.1.x engine
//  was treating 1-2 SECOND errors as if they were drift, when in fact
//  they are CONSTANT OFFSETS that no PI controller can correct.
//
//  Research basis (MDN, W3C, Chrome for Developers, ITU-R BT.1359,
//  EBU R37) plus the realisation that:
//
//    1. A 1-2s error is NOT drift — it's an offset.  No PI controller
//       can fix this; you need a user-configurable offset constant.
//       (This is how DaVinci, Premiere, Resolve all handle it.)
//
//    2. Browsers can SILENTLY DROP seeks.  Setting mediaEl.currentTime=X
//       can fail if the element isn't seekable, if a buffer fill is
//       queued, or if fastSeek is in progress.  You must VERIFY seeks
//       actually took effect.
//
//    3. Raw drift measurements are JITTERY (5-10ms noise at 60Hz).
//       Reacting to raw drift causes oscillation.  EMA-filter first,
//       THEN react.
//
//    4. Correcting based on CURRENT drift is always reactive.  If you
//       also track drift VELOCITY, you can correct based on PREDICTED
//       drift — fixing errors before they become audible.
//
//    5. preservesPitch=true causes the browser to use WSOLA time-
//       stretching when playbackRate != 1.0.  This introduces 20-50ms
//       of hidden buffering latency that the PI controller doesn't
//       know about, causing delayed corrections and overshoot.
//       Toggle preservesPitch=false during correction, restore when
//       settled.
//
//  THE LAYERS (each addresses a different failure mode):
//    LAYER 1: User-configurable audio offset (audioOffsetMs setting)
//    LAYER 2: Verified seek (poll to confirm seek took effect)
//    LAYER 3: EMA-filtered drift + drift velocity + predicted drift
//    LAYER 4: Smart preservesPitch toggling (no WSOLA latency)
//    LAYER 5: Confidence lock (refuse corrections when uncertain)
//    LAYER 6: Hidden-tab dead reckoning (predict video time when rvfc stops)
//
//  CORRECTION ZONES (v6.2 — tighter, based on EMA-filtered drift):
//    0-2ms:    Ignore (below perceptual threshold)
//    2-5ms:    Observe (record only, no correction)
//    5-15ms:   Soft steering   (+/-0.5% rate, P-only)
//    15-30ms:  Active steering  (+/-1% rate, PI)
//    30-60ms:  Strong steering  (+/-2% rate, PID)
//    60-120ms: Conditional recovery (seek if sudden, steer if gradual)
//    120ms+:   Hard seek (immediate reposition)
//
//  PERCEPTIBILITY (ITU-R BT.1359, EBU R37):
//    |drift| < 45ms audio-lagging:  imperceptible
//    |drift| < 125ms audio-lagging: perceptible to trained listeners
//    |drift| > 125ms:               perceptible to everyone
//    audio-leading is detected ~2.5x more easily than audio-lagging
// ── v7.0: TRUE NUCLEAR SYNC ENGINE CONFIG ─────────────────────────
