    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.8.0: THE SITE NATIVE ROUND — (1) THE SITE MIRROR THEME: the overlays now mirror the host site\'s own settings-menu look, live-measured on both sites this round — YouTube\'s frosted-glass player menu (the served www-player.css: radius 12px, blur 16px, 48px rows, hover rgba(255,255,255,.1), Roboto) and Facebook\'s own :root design tokens read off the live permalink (--surface-background, --primary-text #050505, --secondary-text #65676B, --accent #0866FF, the Segoe UI stack); dark AND light variants resolve at runtime from the sites\' own signals (YT\'s html[dark] attribute; FB\'s __fb-dark-mode/__fb-light-mode classes — live-verified), re-resolved at every build, access and geometry settle; unknown hosts fall back to the OLED set; a stored OLED factory pick migrates to Site Mirror while deliberate picks survive. (2) DUET, REDEFINED: OFF by default — the script\'s audio commands; a TRIPLE-TAP on the switch arms the after-script release (once the script\'s audio finishes and the video runs past it, the original unmutes BY ITSELF; a seek back re-seals; a video change disarms; the v9.7 hold valve is retired — the user redefined the ask); the stored both-play flag migrates to false. (3) THE OVERWHELM DOT moved INTO the overlays: the same calculated head-corner point (top 7 / right 8 — inside the padding frame, clear of every interactive element, on the title\'s optical line, stable across the flip) on Slider Syntax\'s BOTH faces and on Stats Syntax; the canvas-corner wrapper dot is retired. (4) THE PROFILE FAMILY GOES LIVE: a Pure Raw / profile change while playing rebuilds the chain under the playing source with a 3ms crossfade — no stop, no reset (the load-reducing Pure Raw off was the exact case the old reset got backwards). (5) THE MENU OPAQUE factory is 100 — the opaque, site-native pane (the v29 bare-glass zero era ends).');
    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.7.1: THE AUDIO COMMAND, COMPLETED — the battery\'s three residual leaks, sealed: (1) ELEMENT-SCOPED MUTE OWNERSHIP: the authored duet mute now carries its element (_duetMutedEl) — at a video change the teardown\'s restore resolves vwatch.current, which is ALREADY the fresh element, and v9.7.0\'s global flag un-muted a fresh autoplay-muted FB reel with the OLD session\'s authored-mute (the reel-swap leak: extMuted misread, the tracker seeded from residue, the restart never re-claiming); the restore now lands on the element we actually muted, returning it to the SITE\'S OWN INTENT (the external tracker) — a reel the site muted for autoplay no longer blasts when the engine leaves, and the engine-off restore of a user-unmuted player is unchanged. (2) THE ENGAGE CLAIM: engagePlayback (the session-start path for an already-playing video — the normal user path, and every reel-swap restart) never applied the duet policy; only the arbiter\'s startAudio did — duet-off left the original audio running until the next enforcement point; the claim now rides the engage leg with the same ordering. (3) THE HOLD-COMMAND RULE: an arbiter hold (out-of-range, seek, ad) flips isPlaying false while the lifecycle state stays \'playing\' — the old duetCommandActive dropped out of command at exactly that moment, so the HOLD VALVE\'S OWN GATE (duetAudioExhausted) read false past the audio\'s end and refused to open, and the claim skipped on holds; a live session is in command for its whole life, held or not. Plus: the mirror\'s MUTE direction snaps to silence (a 10ms ramp from 1.0 leaked a ~30ms decaying blip of our audio at engine start under a muted container — "played regardless", in miniature), and lc.onVideoChange re-seeds the external tracker on the new element so the API reads the fresh element\'s truth.');
    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.7.0: THE AUDIO COMMAND + THE MINIMUM INDICATION — (1) DUET IN COMMAND, CONTINUOUSLY: two sealed root causes behind "the script isn\'t aware of whether duet is toggled on or not". (a) THE SETTINGS DESYNC: the menu seam persisted the duet key but left graph.settings.duet stale until the next session start, so onPlay and the video-change leg kept enforcing the policy the user had just flipped away from — audio passed, the next enforcement point muted it back; the seam now moves the in-memory truth at the toggle (and persists directly — a discrete action needs no debounce). (b) THE LEAK WINDOW: "an unmute outside the 1.5s post-seek window is always respected" let the site players\' own unmutes through (they clear video.muted at times of their own choosing, not only across seeks); the command is now enforced on every volumechange, play, seek, video change AND the earned-cadence sweep (the guard window is retired), while the user\'s player-control intent is honoured on OUR audio through the external mirror — the site\'s controls still govern what is heard. (2) THE DUET HOLD VALVE (the user\'s spec): hold the Duet switch ~700ms while the video outlasts the script\'s audio and our audio can no longer match it → the original audio is released for exactly as long as the hold lasts; releasing re-seals duet\'s command with the pre-valve external mute intent restored underneath; a hold while our audio still matches only peeks the data-info and says so on the head line. (3) THE EXTERNAL VOLUME TRUTH (Facebook): live-verified on the permalink — the video boots muted=true volume=1 playing, the Unmute/Mute buttons write video.muted directly, every real change fires volumechange, a no-change press fires nothing; the old mirror read the raw element and could not tell OUR duet mute from the site\'s own, so an autoplay-muted container read as "ours" and the script played regardless. The new authored-write-tracked external state (_extMuted/_extVol, seeded at element adoption, attribution via the _duetMuted oracle) carries the site\'s intent underneath our mute; the mirror and the gain follow IT. (4) THE MINIMUM INDICATION: a refused overlay access (canvas below the dominance minimum) no longer shows a note — the All Button\'s dynamic bar carries it: a fast flash (300ms, 1 to 0.15) exiting into the listening-hold rhythm (0.8s, 1 to 0.3) for a 2.5s window, then truth resumes; the chip survives only as the no-bar fallback (never a dead gesture).');
    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.6.0: THE OPTIMIZATION RELEASE — (1) EARNED CADENCES: the truth bus (100ms alive / 250ms idle / 500ms overwhelmed), the All Button sweep (250ms alive / 500ms idle / 1s overwhelmed) and the §19 scrambler sweep (250ms alive / 500ms bound / 1s unbound) are self-scheduling chains that snap back to speed on activity, so nothing runs at full cadence while untoggled; the syntax system now builds LAZILY at first access (a page load that never summons it pays zero build cost); the stats loop writes nothing in a hidden tab. (2) THE OVERWHELM WATCH (§15.5): long tasks + a 500ms timer-drift probe + OUR OWN interaction latency (e.timeStamp → handler entry) feed one hysteresis-scored state — when the device drowns, a 3px dot at the very bottom-left of the overlays flashes red (transparent at all other times) and the script degrades ONE STEP AT A TIME: stats 20Hz→150ms, the menu canvas renders every 3rd frame, the typewriter parks, the volume-mirror backstop pauses (the direct volumechange path still runs), and geometry settles wait LONGER — ready visuals, never stuck ones; recovery is gradual by construction (2 hot samples in, 6 cool ones out). (3) THE CANVAS-DOMINANCE GATE (§15.5): the FB non-fullscreen overlay bug the user liked is now intentional law — overlays exist ONLY on a canvas owning >= 75% of the viewport (pure rect measurement, ZERO fullscreen/theater state detection; live-verified both sites: YT default 41% / YT theater 67% / FB permalink 34% / FB reels ~10% refused, fullscreen 100% allowed — the root cause being FB chrome layers in higher stacking contexts painting over any in-canvas anchor); access is refused with a narrated chip (never a dead gesture), and losing the screen while open folds the system with the same gentle fade + note, while a dominant canvas that merely changes SHAPE (rotation in fullscreen) keeps it open. (4) THE SETTLE CHOREOGRAPHY: orientation/resize/fullscreen transitions clear the overlays fast (a 130ms fade), let the browser finish its heavy lifting (320ms, doubled while overwhelmed), then re-anchor + re-fit BOTH overlays and fade them back in slowly (450ms). (5) THE CARRIED FIXES: Stats Syntax is 75% of the canvas height (was 88%); the duet-off seek/skip leak is sealed on both sites — a re-assert that only ever re-mutes a mute WE own (the _duetMuted flag), fired on seeked, on play, inside a 1.5s post-seek guard window on volumechange, and on video change.');
