    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.4.0: §19 THE WEBGL 4-BLOCK SCRAMBLER — the two uploaded userscripts (YouTube + Facebook 4-block scramblers) are one main section: the shared core (shaders, NEAREST-filtered texture, rVFC render loop, rect-copy geometry) plus per-site adapters carrying every site fix (FB tainted-video server re-request with CORS + position restore; YT z-layering + yt-page-data-updated navigation).  It runs when the script is ON (abGlyphOn parity: playing/paused/ad), stays active on pause (frozen scramble; seek-while-paused re-draws the truth), goes completely off on ads and idle (faded out, GL freed, video styles restored), fades in/out as a 300ms opacity CROSSFADE instead of the snap, shows NOTHING until the video is actually playing (armed-on-paused = video fully visible, never black), and the 250ms sweep re-targets vwatch\'s adopted video on removal/replacement — the black-canvas-stuck failure of the standalone scripts is structurally gone.  Zero UI injected, zero site-geometry mutation, TT-safe, fully armored; §16.5/§18 untouched.');
