    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.3.3: §18 HONEST DOWNLOAD-ENTRY DISPLAY + GEOMETRY HARDENING — (a) entering DOWNLOADING now paints the canvas bar IMMEDIATELY as an indeterminate sweep (transparent fill + a 10%-length gradient segment moving back and forth — the head, whichever side leads the travel, at the highest opacity, fading to nothing at the tail; it fully exits the fill head-first then re-enters from that same edge travelling the other way), so a download that has been initiated but has not begun (server slow, 503 in flight) can never look like actual 100% progress; the toggle icon keeps the COMPACT glyph at full opacity with its fill rect hidden, and the ON-clip fill animation starts only when REAL bytes arrive — (b) REAL-BYTE GATE: onProgress bytes paint progress only when the total matches the HEAD content-length (now captured and published to §18.1 as dl meta) or the body is >= 1 KiB (the real error bodies on the source are tiny plaintext — a 404 is 14 B), so the 503 error-page bytes that used to paint a fake full fill on the canvas bar, the icon rect and the speed sampler are ignored entirely — (c) the canvas bar\'s ERROR display now has a LIFECYCLE: 5 seconds after the tier flash paints, the bar returns on its own to its idle/pre-toggle state (the error message stays in the label/tooltip — truth is never lost, only the alarm goes quiet) — (d) GEOMETRY HARDENING: the glyph snap is now two-axis (bottom edge on a device row AND left edge on a device column) and the dynamic bar\'s left/right edges are the glyph\'s painted edges snapped to the SAME device grid (it spans exactly the toggle icon\'s painted length, aligned within one device pixel — the Chromium sub-pixel skew is gone), plus a 250ms sweep-time drift heal re-checks every bar\'s stamped relationship to the glyph so pages that move or re-stamp the player chrome without firing resize (the YouTube-mobile vertical misalignment) heal within one sweep, and the relayout installer now also listens to orientationchange (with settle passes) and visualViewport resize (pinch zoom).');
