    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.2.2: MOBILE-YT PLAYER-COLLAPSE FIX — buildDebugOverlay() stamped an inline position:relative onto #movie_player on EVERY build (its guard read the inline style, which is always empty on a stylesheet-positioned element). On m.youtube.com that inline relative beat the stylesheet .player-container .html5-video-player { position:absolute; inset:0 } — the player\'s ONLY geometry source (parent #player is heightless without padding-bottom:56.25%) — so #movie_player collapsed to 0 height (390×219 → 390×0, reproduced live) and YouTube sized the <video> from the empty box: video canvas destroyed on every page load. Desktop YT was a no-op (#movie_player is natively relative) and FB never hits #movie_player. Overlay anchoring now judges by the COMPUTED position (relative/absolute/fixed/sticky anchors are already containing blocks — the guard the re-anchor path always used; the build path now matches) and NEVER writes inline geometry onto #movie_player: YouTube owns that element\'s positioning on every surface. Net effect: the script no longer mutates site-owned player geometry anywhere — m.youtube.com sees zero mutations, desktop YT unchanged (write was a no-op before), FB unchanged (positioned ancestors were never written; static fallback parents still get the relative nudge).');
