    log('INFO', 'Boot', 'v9.0.1: THE DETECTIVE ENGINE (chaos-hardened: armored reads, unreadable-time strike rule, ground-truth seek watcher, instant ad-shrink suspicion). Base v9.0.0: — (1) 16ms ground-truth heartbeat: reads video/paused/rate/duration/src/ctx directly, events are hints not truth; (2) strike rule: 5 consecutive missed video-time reads (~83ms) hard-stop audio, 2 good reads release it; (3) ONE arbiter owns every start/stop via ordered hold-reasons (lifecycle, video-gone, src-change, time-lost, video-paused, video-ended, rate0, ad, seek-hold, out-of-range, ctx-suspended, no-buffer); (4) out-of-range = HARD PAUSE, no hysteresis: videoTime past the audio buffer holds audio until the video returns to a matchable time; (5) six detectors: silent-events (synthesizes dropped pause/play/rate/seek/ended), phantom-correction (verifies every steering action against predicted drift response; step-jumps discarded; distrust + safe mode), unmarked-ad (duration-fingerprint + src-swap suspicion, holds until content returns), ctx-suspended (frozen-clock detection, resume campaign, realign), src-change (videoId/currentSrc fingerprint, instant hold on navigation), recovery-thrash (restart-rate window, escalating cooldown, decay on stability); (6) performPhaseRecovery is thrash-guarded, cooldown-deferred and VERIFIED after landing; (7) v8.4 fixes: _seeking never cleared on seeked (drift correction died after first seek), watchdog/ENDED restarted audio beyond the buffer range, seeked-while-paused started audio, missed playing/canplay left audio dead forever, ad-resume ignored range, dead statechange listener, never-called stopSyncHealthWatchdog.');
